Datatypes? - To control the entry of data type/to represent the type of data.
*INT() - whole numbers - to represent Number type eg: Empl_ID
*VARCHAR(10) - represent the data type as a string max of 10 characters which means any string data should be in limit of 10 characters only .it depends of requirement
*DATE - entry type should be date format "YYYY-MM-DD"
*TIMESTAMP - entry should be date with timestamp "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS"
*BLOB - Binary large object type.
*DECIMAL(3,2) - the type of the data should be decimal - the decimal values should be 2 digits after the 3 integer values eg: 325.25


constraints?
*UNIQUE - The data in the column should be unique with no duplicates.
*NOT NULL - To avoid NULL values
*DEFAULT - when the entry is not done it should be value of default value.   eg : DEFAULT "active"
*AUTO_INCREMENT - to assign number as sequence automatically without specifically define them.



Primary key?
*unique value to represent each entry of the row.
*should not be null and no duplicates.
eg:emp_id

foreign key?
*connects between 2 tables
*the primary key of one table be foreign key of another table.

unique key?
*unique value to prevent duplicates entries of the column
*eg: email_id,phone_number,SSN

surrogate key?
*generate by system
*has no business meaning.
*uniquely identify each entry of the data.
eg:order_id

Natural key?
*no system generated key.
*has business meaning.
*generally available in real time
eg:email_id, phone_number

composite key?
*combination of 2 columns as a unique identifier of the table
*if there is no unique value in table by a single column . we may combine 2 columns to identify the record of the table
eg:primary key(student_id,course_id) - a single student can enroll multiple courses and a single course can be enrolled by multiple students.
                                    - But no same student can enroll same course twice. Here, with student_id or course_id alone is not enough to identify unique record ,
                                    but with the help of the both columns we can easily represent unique value.

