wildcards? - commands
* LIKE - used to find pattern of the record/data/entry.
* % - used to print the data as a pattern - Any no.of characters be there before and after the desired data. it wil dispaly all data where it macthes the respective "%" defined pattern.
  eg: select * from employee
      where emp_name LIKE "%John%";
  it will print all records wherever the entries is included as "john" - it doesn't matter weather any no.of characters are there before and after of the name john.
* _ - underscore used to print as a pattern ,but it represents exact no.of characters before and after the desired record.
  eg: select * from employee
      where emp_name LIKE "_John_" - means it prints the records with a single character before and after of the john.

select * from employee
where emp_name LIKE "__john%" - it displays all records with exact charecters before of the john and any number of characters afetr john name .


