joins?
*The joins are basically combine of two table rows.
*Joins can be done as reference with the comman column in the both tables.
Types:
1)inner join : Returns the common rows in both tables. By default the inner join will be executed if we don't specify join type.
2)left join : returns the all rows from left table and common rows from the right table. unmatched columns will return as "NULL"
3)right join : returns the all rows from the right table and common rows from the left table.
4)full outer join : return all rows from both tables and unmatched rows as well ,regardless of matched rows or not.

triggers?
*A trigger is an database object that automatically executes a block of sql code when a specific events occurs on atable or view.
*trigerrs are the query which we can executed automatically in database.
*basically used when there are any events are done in the tables.
*it sipmly called as automation in the database for the events

eg syntax:

create trigger trigger_name {before|after} {insert|update|delete}
