er diagram(Entity relationship diagram)?
*Visual representation of a database structure that shows how data is organized and how diff pieces of data are related to each other.
*this should be helpful before creating a database to understand what are the table_names and data types and how the relation is defined b/w tables.
in this er dig we have:
1)entity   - which is also called table_names    -  represented as rectangle
2)attributes - the columns in the tables (primary,derived,simple attribute) - represented as ovals
3)relationship - refer by primary and foreign keys - represented with diamond symbol 
4)cardinality - one - one ,one-many and many - many relationship - representes as 1:1, 1:N, N:M
5)weak entity - it cannot identified by its own attributes - so we can identify with the help of parent primary key which is a foreign key in the table or else combination of keys.- represented as double rectangle























